{"type":"message","id":"d2614d36","parentId":"153a467c","timestamp":"2026-03-21T00:41:01.667Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The read failed because I used an absolute path - the file is at /home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/AGENTS.md relative to the workspace root.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=read>\n<parameter=path>\n/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/AGENTS.md\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"b44d2b85-0d1d-4da1-89ae-1d93090ed5c5","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/AGENTS.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"mlx-community/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-4bit","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774053638810}}
{"type":"message","id":"5ea2a315","parentId":"d2614d36","timestamp":"2026-03-21T00:41:01.694Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"b44d2b85-0d1d-4da1-89ae-1d93090ed5c5","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Available Agents\n\n## coder\n- **Specialty**: Software engineering, script generation, filesystem ops, shell execution, git operations.\n- **When to use**: Any request requiring code implementation, bug fixing, file manipulation, or command execution.\n- **Spawn with**: `sessions_spawn` targeting agent `coder`.\n- **Always set**: `deliver: false` so the coder replies to YOU, not the user.\n\n## reviewer\n- **Specialty**: Code review, security auditing, static analysis, anti-pattern detection.\n- **When to use**: ALWAYS after coder returns a code payload, BEFORE returning results to the user.\n- **Spawn with**: `sessions_spawn` targeting agent `reviewer`.\n- **Always set**: `deliver: false` so the reviewer replies to YOU, not the user.\n- **On REJECT**: Use `sessions_send` to pass reviewer feedback to the coder's existing session for fixes.\n- **On APPROVE**: Instruct coder to commit and push to a feature branch, then report to user.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774053661690}}
{"type":"message","id":"b8cba20f","parentId":"5ea2a315","timestamp":"2026-03-21T00:41:27.817Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the agent structure and can propose a clear step-by-step plan for the livesport.cz football dashboard project, asking Klaus for confirmations and requirements before spawning the coder agent.\n</think>\n\nPerfect. I've got the agent setup. Here's the plan for your livesport.cz live football dashboard:\n\n**Phase 1:** Research livesport.cz structure and rate limits, then build a scraper that fetches live football matches.\n\n**Phase 2:** Set up an in-memory cache (with optional Redis for persistence) to keep data fresh.\n\n**Phase 3:** Build a simple web dashboard (React/Vue or Flask/FastAPI + static HTML) to display live matches.\n\n**Phase 4:** Add auto-refresh and real-time updates.\n\nBefore I kick off the coder agent, I need to know:\n\n1. **Preferred stack?** Python (FastAPI/Flask) or JavaScript/TypeScript (Next.js/Express)?\n2. **How fresh should data be?** Every 30 seconds? Every minute? Real-time polling?\n3. **What data points matter?** Score, time, league, teams, maybe stats like shots/corners?\n\nGive me your preferences and I'll get the coder agent working immediately"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"mlx-community/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-4bit","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774053661695}}
{"type":"message","id":"fb2da5ff","parentId":"b8cba20f","timestamp":"2026-03-21T00:42:33.998Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"2514\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8437938758\",\n  \"sender\": \"Klaus Ampler\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-21 00:42 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Klaus Ampler (8437938758)\",\n  \"id\": \"8437938758\",\n  \"name\": \"Klaus Ampler\",\n  \"username\": \"klausampler\"\n}\n```\n\nFastAPI sounds good, data every 30s, but configurable, start with score, time, league tesms and make it extendsble?"}],"timestamp":1774053753996}}
{"type":"message","id":"c0346b27","parentId":"fb2da5ff","timestamp":"2026-03-21T00:42:59.808Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"User has confirmed their preferences (FastAPI, 30s refresh, basic data points), so I can now spawn the coder agent with a clear, detailed task specification covering all requirements.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=sessions_spawn>\n<parameter=label>\nlivesport-football-dashboard-coder\n</parameter>\n<parameter=task>\nBuild a FastAPI-based live football dashboard for livesport.cz:\n\n**Requirements:**\n1. **Scraper** - Fetch live football matches from livesport.cz\n   - Extract: teams, score, match time, league, match status (live/halftime/fulltime)\n   - Handle rate limits and anti-scraping measures\n   - Configurable polling interval (default 30s)\n   - Make it extensible for future data points (shots, corners, cards, etc.)\n\n2. **Cache Layer** - In-memory cache with optional Redis\n   - Store latest match data\n   - Auto-refresh on configurable interval (30s default)\n   - Fast lookups for UI\n\n3. **FastAPI Web Dashboard**\n   - REST API endpoints for match data\n   - Simple HTML/CSS/JS dashboard UI showing live matches\n   - Auto-refresh"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"mlx-community/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-4bit","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774053753997}}
